+# Native Operations Integration R1
+
+TASK_ID=FACTORY_OPS_MONITOR_SITE_INTEGRATION_R1
+
+## Provenance and Authorization
+
+- Monitor base: `91b686a313e2f73e0fec9459404ac8ef2b3abc19`.
+- Branch: `codex/factory-ops-monitor-portal-r1`.
+- Canonical local source: `/Users/charles/Documents/监控系统/vue_switch_work`.
+- Remote is `ssh://coldstorageamz/mnt/data/opencode-test`, not GitHub. No SSH
+  fetch/push, remote command, server edit, deploy, Ready or merge was performed.
+- Worktree: `/Users/charles/codex-monitor-portal-r1`. It is selectively materialized
+  because the original source is in cloud-managed storage. All 166 available
+  source files were compared to pinned Git blob IDs before any edit. Unavailable
+  historic previews/docs stay unchanged in the commit tree, not deleted.
+- Backups: `/Users/charles/factory-ops-monitor-r1-backup/`, private permissions.
+  Operations main archive SHA256:
+  `4ee45d436ef916d3e4c57d1cab2250f1a458c1e9f8c9b81187e692a1a06f3ddf`.
+  Retained tested monitor source archive SHA256:
+  `13d9de4cd9f698003901cf26918d723bfc20c507166f87c6f1afb58a7cee827e`.
+
+## Implementation
+
+The existing Vue router imports `/operations` from a source export of
+`xuezhiorange-png/factory-operations-platform` at
+`dba043667970e6019dbdc7a8420969d82411d090`. There is no operations iframe, second
+application mount, independent landing page, duplicate dashboard or new monitor
+store. The existing independent Xinshao model is unchanged.
+
+`frontend/vendor/factory-operations-portal/SOURCE.json` records the clean source
+commit and hashes for all 37 reused files. Refresh using the operations repo's
+`scripts/export_monitor_portal.mjs` from a reviewed clean commit, not manual edits
+to vendored business components. Vue/router/icons are resolved by the existing
+Vite dedupe configuration.
+
+PC/header/home-rail and H5 navigation gain an operations entry. The original four
+monitoring H5 entries and account button remain. The factory dialog gains an
+icon link to an exact reviewed gateway identity. Grouped/unknown identities never
+guess a factory by name. Operations-to-monitor return revalidates the personal
+operations session/asset pair, then checks factory/gateway/device against the
+reviewed registry before resolving a current monitor device.
+
+The generated `operations-registry.json` contains only source-defined IDs, no
+telemetry, personal data or credentials. Rebuild it with
+`node scripts/export-operations-registry.cjs` after an approved registry edit.
+Its source hash and complete target-ID sets are regression-tested.
+
+## Authentication and Deployment Gates
+
+Monitor role accounts are not verified personal identities. Unified login is
+BLOCKED. Native operations queries send no monitor Authorization header, use an
+independently verified operations session and keep PostgreSQL factory isolation
+and audit checks on the existing FastAPI side. No shared admin/user-ID workaround.
+No monitor SQLite, Node API, PLC, collection, alert or device-control logic changed.
+
+The development proxy `/operations-api/v1/*` maps to FastAPI `/api/v1/*`.
+`OPERATIONS_API_DEV_TARGET` is a local-development target, not evidence of a free
+production port. No production Nginx location has been installed. The review-only
+example lives in the operations repo under `deploy/monitor-site/`.
+
+Real ID mappings are empty until explicitly reviewed and configured server-side.
+Unknown links show `尚未关联`, never another factory/device's data. Six unfinished
+business modules show `待开发`, not mock business records.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Full monitor tests: 163 passed, no failures/skips (160 existing + 3 new).
+- Existing frontend typecheck and multi-entry Vite build pass. The existing
+  Three.js chunk advisory remains visible; no build threshold was relaxed.
+- Actual App.vue browser checks: desktop1440, tablet768, H5 390/320 widths;
+  native table/detail/return, zero horizontal portal overflow and no module iframe.
+- Original home 3D map rendered, and devices/alarm/energy navigation remained
+  functional with explicitly empty synthetic monitor data. This is not real
+  telemetry, physical-phone, actual control or production-server acceptance.
+- Operations API/PostgreSQL authorization, revocation and ID-mapping tests passed
+  separately. No synthetic session is shipped in production sources.
+- Operations repo delivery evidence contains the detailed source audit,
+  screenshots, rejected compositor captures and exact CI references.
+
+READY_FOR_DEPLOYMENT=NO. Personal SSO, real ID-map approval, user-run PR #10 server
+audit, review, exact-head CI and recoverable deployment backup remain gates.
+
+No production rollback is needed. Revert only this scoped local change for source
+rollback; do not restore a database, change credentials or restart services.
